<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I5d26708977a4ac43c339fb53b124948fc61cb4c2" commit="d222180d7a202927a4e41f3b2e328f286d5df53f" commit_message="Add infra/ci_results_archiver  BUG=chromium:737345 TEST=None CQ-DEPEND=CL:*404328  Change-Id: I5d26708977a4ac43c339fb53b124948fc61cb4c2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/556111 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ningning Xia &lt;nxia@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="556111" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/11/556111/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic10844562def23a9633dd8333ffbd9a75340bf03" commit="11b462e44155d90d73dc819564d5d4f7e4a31b48" commit_message="kahlee: check if battery is present by HW pin  Battery present should be correctly detected even the battery is in ship mode and waked by AC.  BRANCH=None BUG=None TEST=Use &quot;ectool batterycutoff&quot; to enter battery ship mode and plug in type-c adapter to wake battery  Change-Id: Ic10844562def23a9633dd8333ffbd9a75340bf03 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/477813 Commit-Ready: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Lin Cloud &lt;cloud_lin@compal.com&gt; Tested-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: YH Lin &lt;yueherngl@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Martin Roth &lt;martinroth@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="477813" owner_email="cloud_lin@compal.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/13/477813/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I4b05eaa9cabff8117571e93e03f88eb7497d592b" commit="a962bdb53859729e14b5069830f91c9c53e3f8b8" commit_message="UPSTREAM: fs/exec.c: account for argv/envp pointers  When limiting the argv/envp strings during exec to 1/4 of the stack limit, the storage of the pointers to the strings was not included.  This means that an exec with huge numbers of tiny strings could eat 1/4 of the stack limit in strings and then additional space would be later used by the pointers to the strings.  For example, on 32-bit with a 8MB stack rlimit, an exec with 1677721 single-byte strings would consume less than 2MB of stack, the max (8MB / 4) amount allowed, but the pointers to the strings would consume the remaining additional stack space (1677721 * 4 == 6710884).  The result (1677721 + 6710884 == 8388605) would exhaust stack space entirely.  Controlling this stack exhaustion could result in pathological behavior in setuid binaries (CVE-2017-1000365).  [akpm@linux-foundation.org: additional commenting from Kees] Fixes: b6a2fea39318 (&quot;mm: variable length argument support&quot;) Link: http://lkml.kernel.org/r/20170622001720.GA32173@beast Signed-off-by: Kees Cook &lt;keescook@chromium.org&gt; Acked-by: Rik van Riel &lt;riel@redhat.com&gt; Acked-by: Michal Hocko &lt;mhocko@suse.com&gt; Cc: Alexander Viro &lt;viro@zeniv.linux.org.uk&gt; Cc: Qualys Security Advisory &lt;qsa@qualys.com&gt; Cc: &lt;stable@vger.kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton &lt;akpm@linux-foundation.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Linus Torvalds &lt;torvalds@linux-foundation.org&gt;  BUG=chromium:737530 TEST=Build and run  Change-Id: I4b05eaa9cabff8117571e93e03f88eb7497d592b Signed-off-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 98da7d08850fb8bdeb395d6368ed15753304aa0c) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/558189 Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit b766affbe86571886e2740963e3de5c0250af0cd) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/561957 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="561957" owner_email="groeck@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/57/561957/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1479d30eef65d940f265ec995db7ec181642a2ff" commit="878be7c2cf53360925f0601c2e567be786be006f" commit_message="chromiumos-sdk: use lumpy to replace x86-generic in test.  We have deprecated x86 boards, so we can remove x86-generic from chromiumos-sdk now. We added lumpy because it contains some au code built with i686 toolchain.  BUG=chromium:738137 TEST=run_test passes.  Change-Id: I1479d30eef65d940f265ec995db7ec181642a2ff Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/556403 Commit-Ready: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Yunlian Jiang &lt;yunlian@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="556403" owner_email="yunlian@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/03/556403/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.8" change_id="Ie966d977205a894c5c55c0a27f7f61003a85960b" commit="c3c113acc57e1064bcd6fe52688598a283eacb21" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dccp: fix freeing skb too early for IPV6_RECVPKTINFO  In the current DCCP implementation an skb for a DCCP_PKT_REQUEST packet is forcibly freed via __kfree_skb in dccp_rcv_state_process if dccp_v6_conn_request successfully returns.  However, if IPV6_RECVPKTINFO is set on a socket, the address of the skb is saved to ireq-&gt;pktopts and the ref count for skb is incremented in dccp_v6_conn_request, so skb is still in use. Nevertheless, it gets freed in dccp_rcv_state_process.  Fix by calling consume_skb instead of doing goto discard and therefore calling __kfree_skb.  Similar fixes for TCP:  fb7e2399ec17f1004c0e0ccfd17439f8759ede01 [TCP]: skb is unexpectedly freed. 0aea76d35c9651d55bbaf746e7914e5f9ae5a25d tcp: SYN packets are now simply consumed  BUG=b:63333486 TEST=None  Signed-off-by: Andrey Konovalov &lt;andreyknvl@google.com&gt; Acked-by: Eric Dumazet &lt;edumazet@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5edabca9d4cff7f1f2b68f0bac55ef99d9798ba4) Signed-off-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: Ie966d977205a894c5c55c0a27f7f61003a85960b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/560013 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="560013" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/13/560013/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia28481414b5db8b413d70839076ddcc50d747f6e" commit="808897daa8abc95e8582121b30985b9b5960a570" commit_message="[autotest] Delay chromite imports in site_utils  The chromite imports in site_utils are specific to some specialized use-cases, but cost all users 2-3 seconds total during module import. This was a bottleneck in the scheduler tick time.  The correct fix is to break apart server/site_utils since it does way too much. The hack is to delay the imports.  BUG=chromium:739466 TEST=None  Change-Id: Ia28481414b5db8b413d70839076ddcc50d747f6e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/559831 Commit-Ready: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Prathmesh Prabhu &lt;pprabhu@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Xixuan Wu &lt;xixuan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="559831" owner_email="pprabhu@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/31/559831/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7ea94785a382128b30755013322e45cd16922782" commit="5fd63156cb4372b88d6967eb81899523cfffe160" commit_message="debugd: Add SetCapabilities to SandboxedProcess  Add a SetCapabilities method that adds a &quot;-c &lt;caps&gt;&quot; minijail0 argument, allowing the capabilities of the SandboxedProcess to be restricted.  BUG=chromium:739400 TEST=debugd test TEST=use SandboxedProcess to run iw with CAP_NET_ADMIN  Change-Id: I7ea94785a382128b30755013322e45cd16922782 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/560536 Commit-Ready: Edward Hill &lt;ecgh@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Edward Hill &lt;ecgh@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Jorge Lucangeli Obes &lt;jorgelo@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="560536" owner_email="ecgh@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/36/560536/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4b3cd0627ecaa248e18413a84200681bae741fb3" commit="d460e094ba12e037d790839dbcfbc81015a0f6d3" commit_message="autotest-server: adds cloud console proto compilation.  BUG=chromium:736841 TEST=manual.  Change-Id: I4b3cd0627ecaa248e18413a84200681bae741fb3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/549778 Commit-Ready: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Keith Haddow &lt;haddowk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="549778" owner_email="ntang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/78/549778/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.10" change_id="Ie966d977205a894c5c55c0a27f7f61003a85960b" commit="bb3c53db54cf4f2061d3be038db5bc6c35e43115" commit_message="UPSTREAM: dccp: fix freeing skb too early for IPV6_RECVPKTINFO  In the current DCCP implementation an skb for a DCCP_PKT_REQUEST packet is forcibly freed via __kfree_skb in dccp_rcv_state_process if dccp_v6_conn_request successfully returns.  However, if IPV6_RECVPKTINFO is set on a socket, the address of the skb is saved to ireq-&gt;pktopts and the ref count for skb is incremented in dccp_v6_conn_request, so skb is still in use. Nevertheless, it gets freed in dccp_rcv_state_process.  Fix by calling consume_skb instead of doing goto discard and therefore calling __kfree_skb.  Similar fixes for TCP:  fb7e2399ec17f1004c0e0ccfd17439f8759ede01 [TCP]: skb is unexpectedly freed. 0aea76d35c9651d55bbaf746e7914e5f9ae5a25d tcp: SYN packets are now simply consumed  BUG=b:63333486 TEST=None  Signed-off-by: Andrey Konovalov &lt;andreyknvl@google.com&gt; Acked-by: Eric Dumazet &lt;edumazet@google.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David S. Miller &lt;davem@davemloft.net&gt; (cherry picked from commit 5edabca9d4cff7f1f2b68f0bac55ef99d9798ba4) Signed-off-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@google.com&gt;  Change-Id: Ie966d977205a894c5c55c0a27f7f61003a85960b Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/560012 Commit-Ready: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Bernie Thompson &lt;bhthompson@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Guenter Roeck &lt;groeck@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="560012" owner_email="bhthompson@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/cha